   "summary": "Fears that the artificial intelligence (AI) investment cycle may be nearing its peak triggered a wave of panic selling in semiconductor stocks, Friday, sending shares of Korea’s two chipmaking giants, Samsung Electronics and SK hynix, plunging nearly 10 percent. As of 10:30 a.m., SK hynix had tumbled 10.28 percent, while Samsung Electronics had fallen 7.99 percent.",
   "summary_zh": "人工智能（AI）投资周期可能即将见顶的担忧，周五引发了半导体股票抛售潮，使韩国两大芯片制造商三星电子和SK海力士的股价暴跌近10%。截至上午10时30分，SK海力士下跌10.28%，三星电子下跌7.99%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Fears that the artificial intelligence (AI) investment cycle may be nearing its peak triggered a wave of panic selling in semiconductor stocks, Friday, sending shares of Korea’s two chipmaking giants, Samsung Electronics and SK hynix, plunging nearly 10 percent. As of 10:30 a.m., SK hynix had tumbled 10.28 percent, while Samsung Electronics had fallen 7.99 percent. The benchmark KOSPI opened 2.24 percent lower at 5,263.26 before triggering a circuit breaker just three minutes into the session, which temporarily suspends trading for 20 minutes when market movements become too volatile and breach a certain threshold. The index subsequently plunged more than 8 percent, falling below the 5,000 mark for the first time in 10 months since January",
