   "_dt": 1793933524.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung was set to hold a summit with East Timorese President Jose Ramos-Horta on Friday to discuss ways to strengthen cooperation between their countries. Horta, the 1996 recipient of the Nobel Peace Prize, arrived in Korea the previous day for a three-day trip at Lee's invitation, marking the first visit to Korea by an East Timorese leader since the two countries established diplomatic relations in 2002.",
   "summary_zh": "李在明总统定于周五与东帝汶总统何塞·拉莫斯-奥尔塔举行峰会，讨论加强两国合作的方法。奥尔塔是1996年诺贝尔和平奖得主，他应李在明邀请于前一天抵达韩国，开启为期三天的行程。这是自2007年两国建立外交关系以来东帝汶领导人首次访问韩国。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung was set to hold a summit with East Timorese President Jose Ramos-Horta on Friday to discuss ways to strengthen cooperation between their countries. Horta, the 1996 recipient of the Nobel Peace Prize, arrived in Korea the previous day for a three-day trip at Lee's invitation, marking the first visit to Korea by an East Timorese leader since the two countries established diplomatic relations in 2002. During Friday's summit, the two leaders are expected to discuss ways to enhance cooperation in sectors ranging from security, intellectual property, climate change and education to human exchanges while exchanging views on regional security and the latest international issues. They will also attend a signing ceremony for memorandums of understanding between their countries and a joint press announcement at Cheong Wa Dae",
