   "summary": "Oluchi Chibuzor Lagos Free Zone,has called for stronger investment partnerships between Nigerian, Belgian and Luxembourg businesses to accelerate trade relationships, local manufacturing, agro-processing and industrial development that create jobs and retain more economic value in Nigeria. The call was made by the Managing Director of Lagos Free Zone, Adesuwa Ladoja, during her keynote address at the Nigeria–Belgium–Luxembourg Business Forum, which held in Brussels from 28–30 October 2026.",
   "summary_zh": "拉各斯自由区首席执行官Oluchi Chibuzor呼吁加强尼日利亚、比利时和卢森堡企业之间的投资伙伴关系，以加快贸易关系发展，推动本地制造业、农业加工和工业发展，在尼日利亚创造就业机会并留住更多经济价值。拉各斯自由区首席执行官Adesuwa Ladoja在2026年10月28日至30日于布鲁塞尔举行的尼日利亚—比利时—卢森堡商业论坛主旨演讲中发出这一呼吁。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Oluchi Chibuzor Lagos Free Zone,has called for stronger investment partnerships between Nigerian, Belgian and Luxembourg businesses to accelerate trade relationships, local manufacturing, agro-processing and industrial development that create jobs and retain more economic value in Nigeria. The call was made by the Managing Director of Lagos Free Zone, Adesuwa Ladoja, during her keynote address at the Nigeria–Belgium–Luxembourg Business Forum, which held in Brussels from 28–30 October 2026. Ladoja highlighted the complementary strengths of the three countries, noting that Nigeria’s natural resources, talent and market potential, alongside Belgium’s manufacturing expertise and trade connections and Luxembourg’s industrial and financial capabilities, create significant opportunities for mutually beneficial investment. She emphasised that stronger cross-border partnerships could help Nigeria",
