   "title": "US Midterm Elections Produce Historic First For Black Governors",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/us-midterm-elections-produce-historic-first-for-black-governors/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 08:43:16 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793781796.0,
   "ageDays": 1.77,
   "summary": "Hours later, David Crowley also secured victory in Wisconsin’s gubernatorial race, becoming the fourth Black politician to win a governorship in Tuesday’s elections. The development marks a significant moment in American political history, as no two elected Black governors had previously served at the same time. Before Tuesday’s victories, only three Black politicians had been elected governors in the United States.",
   "summary_zh": "几小时后，David Crowley也在威斯康星州州长选举中获胜，成为周二选举中第四位赢得州长职位的黑人政治家。这一进展标志着美国政治史上的重要时刻，因为此前从未有两位当选的黑人州长同时任职。在周二获胜之前，美国仅有三位黑人政治家当选州长。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The victories followed wins by Democratic Governor Wes Moore in Maryland, Republican Representative Byron Donalds in Florida and Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms in Georgia. Hours later, David Crowley also secured victory in Wisconsin’s gubernatorial race, becoming the fourth Black politician to win a governorship in Tuesday’s elections. The development marks a significant moment in American political history, as no two elected Black governors had previously served at the same time. Before Tuesday’s victories, only three Black politicians had been elected governors in the United States. They were Moore, who was elected governor of Maryland; Deval Patrick, a Democrat who won the Massachusetts governorship in 2006; and Doug Wilder, who made history in 1989 as the first Black governor of Virginia. “From a larger perspective, there’s so much that has been talked about in politics over the last couple decades around race. Obviously, the country has had some real negative parts of our history surrounding race,” he said. Meanwhile, the number of Black politicians who could join the historic group may increase, depending on the outcome of another gubernatorial contest. Nevada Attorney General Aaron Ford, a Black Democrat, is also seeking to become governor, challenging incumbent Republican Governor Joe Lombardo. However, several other Black candidates failed to secure victories in their respective gubernatorial contests. In South Carolina, Democratic State Representative Jermaine Johnson lost the governorship to Republican Alan Wilson. Similarly, Republican Representative John James lost his gubernatorial bid to Democrat Jocelyn Benson, while Minnesota State House Speaker Lisa Demuth was defeated by Democrat Amy Klobuchar. The victories mark a significant development in the representation of Black Americans in the country’s highest state executive offices. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af",
    "wa"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
