   "title": "Nigeria and the United States have pledged stronger intelligence sharing and law enforcement cooperation against cybercrime, sextortion and",
   "url": "https://x.com/voiceofnigeria/status/2117522807609303227",
   "snippet": "Nigeria and the United States have pledged stronger intelligence sharing and law enforcement cooperation against cybercrime, sextortion and romance scams. During Nigeria’s Cybercrime Awareness Week in Abuja, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State Michael Gonzales met officials from @officialEFCC, the National Security Adviser’s office, @ndlea_nigeria and @PoliceNG, urging closer coordination to tackle criminals operating across borders.\n\nGonzales said cooperation must move beyond arrests to dismantle criminal networks and trace their finances. FBI’s Abuja office and Nigerian authorities have secured 41 extraditions since 2022, including five in 2026. In August, Nigeria extradited two alleged cybercriminals in separate sextortion cases involving US minors.\n\n#Nigeria #UnitedStates #Cybercrime #Sextortion #RomanceScams",
   "body": "Nigeria and the United States have pledged stronger intelligence sharing and law enforcement cooperation against cybercrime, sextortion and romance scams. During Nigeria’s Cybercrime Awareness Week in Abuja, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State Michael Gonzales met officials from @officialEFCC, the National Security Adviser’s office, @ndlea_nigeria and @PoliceNG, urging closer coordination to tackle criminals operating across borders.\n\nGonzales said cooperation must move beyond arrests to dismantle criminal networks and trace their finances. FBI’s Abuja office and Nigerian authorities have secured 41 extraditions since 2022, including five in 2026. In August, Nigeria extradited two alleged cybercriminals in separate sextortion cases involving US minors.\n\n#Nigeria #UnitedStates #Cybercrime #Sextortion #RomanceScams",
